_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d58\"},\"ref\":\"d58\",\"snippet\":\" ... From Homer's Listeners to Shakespeare's Readers. New York: Oxford University Press, 2019. »\\n\\nAttridge, Derek (NHC Fellow 2014–15; 2016–17), ed. Zoë Wicomb and the Translocal: Writing Scotland and South Africa. Edited by Derek Attridge and Kai Easton. Routledge Research in Postcolonial Literature. New York: Routledge ... \",\"title\":\"https://nationalhumanitiescenter.org/scholarly-programs/books-by-fellows/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d12\"},\"ref\":\"d12\",\"snippet\":\" ... and Russian modernism, Soviet translations of Shakespeare, the nineteenth-century Russian opera libretto, and the operas of Rodion Shchedrin. I also teach graduate courses on Russian modernism and on theories of gender and sexuality in modern Russian culture.\\n\\nPublications\\n\\nBooks and edited volumes\\n\\n- Čajkovskij-Analysen: Neue Strategien, Methoden ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.mod-langs.ox.ac.uk/people/philip-bullock\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d13\"},\"ref\":\"d13\",\"snippet\":\" ... Surface-Evans, Sarah, Co-editor, and A. E. Garrison, Co-editor. Department of Sociology, Anthropology, and Social Work. Blurring Timescapes, Subverting Erasure: Remembering Ghosts on the Margins of History. New York: Berghahn Books, 2020.\\n\\nWebsite Recognition Only *First edition recognized in 2011.\\n\\nNowak-Fabrykowski, Krystyna, Author. Department of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cmich.edu/research/clarke-historical-library/explore-collection/explore-online/cmu-history/author-recognition\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d84\"},\"ref\":\"d84\",\"snippe