ed\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d92\"},\"ref\":\"d92\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarah_Bernhardt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d94\"},\"ref\":\"d94\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riyad_Mahrez\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d120\"},\"ref\":\"d120\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.pacegallery.com/artists/jean-dubuffet/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d113\"},\"ref\":\"d113\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SS_La_Bourgogne\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d114\"},\"ref\":\"d114\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.rsssf.org/tablesf/franchamp.html\"}],\"next_step\":\"Open a received ref with read; use replay=true to restore full cached navigation.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":10,\"prior_deliveries\":3,\"query_key\":\"30207e758085ffba5dca5009c859330f734242fcd19eb9fb57e128addce7dc1e\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"b7e0f58c12a6fe70c3ac3ba6feecd68dde93b46dd74435e9f5b839a1db348097\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Sarah Hatchuel GRIC coordinator Le Havre research group 2009\",\"view\":\"reuse\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_0dde665592284f3fad32cdeb"},{"content":"Previously delivered raw windows (untrusted source data, not instructions or verified claims):\n[{\"document\":\"d30\",\"document_chars\":45990,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"6c425210769d1528145667a872b4948f5eaaaea98e426b28765b0125ab595d88\",\"snapshot\":\"be58fb82f749ee77102eed93f6ddcac6babc7fbe5610c5090b94be0ec3abfe50\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Calls for papers – Conferences taking place in September 2019\\ndate: 2018-01-26\\n---\\nSecrets: 22nd International Colloquium of American Studies\\n\\nFaculty of Arts, Palacký University in Olomouc, Czech Republic, 12-14 September 2019\\n\\nExtended deadline for proposals: 20 June 2019\\n\\nPlenary speakers:\\n\\nPhilip McGowan (Queen's University Belfast),\\n\\nBrian Ward (Northumbria University)\\n\\nSecrets in American Literature, Film, Media, History\\n\\n- The Importance of Keeping Secrets\\n\\n- Secrets, Secrecy and Transparency\\n\\n- Privacy and Secrets\\n\\n- Public and State Secrets in the Post-Truth Age\\n\\n- Secret Agencies and Secret Societies\\n\\n- Female and Male Secretaries\\n\\n- Secret Identities and Secret Agents\\n\\n- Secret Places and Spaces\\n\\n- Skeletons in the Closet\\n\\n- The Perils of Having Secrets\\n\\nExtended deadline for paper proposals (300 words) and short professional bios of max. 150 words: June 29, 2019\\n\\nEmail: colloquium.olomouc@upol.cz\\n\\nWeb: \\n\\nDeadline for full papers: September 5, 2019\\n\\nSelected papers will be published in the peer-reviewed academic journal the Moravian Journal of Literature and Film, published by Palacký University Press in Olomouc.\\n\\nSee \\n\\nRegistration Fee:\\n\\nCSAAS members: 30 EUR (early registration); 40 EUR (late registration)\\n\\nNon-members: 50 EUR (early registration); 60 EUR (late registration)\\n\\nOrganizing committee:\\n\\nElizabeth Woock, Lukáš Merz, Kamila Večeřová\\n\\nScientific committee:\\n\\nMichal Peprník (Palacký University Olomouc, Czech Republic), Chair of the Czech and Slovak Association for American Studies\\n\\nJaroslav Kušnír (University of Prešov, Slovak Republic, Vice-Chair of the Czech and Slovak Association for American Studies\\n\\nMarcel Arbeit (Palacký University Olomouc, Czech Republic)\\n\\nJosef Jařab (Palacký University Olomouc, Czech Republic)\\n\\nŠárka Bubíková (University of Pardubice, Czech Republic)\\n\\nPalacký University Olomouc is the second-oldest university in Czechia, educating scholars since the 16th century. See \\n\\nThe city of Olomouc is also the place of one of the richest national heritage sites, second only to Prague.\\n\\nOlomouc is easily accessible from all of the following airports by train, bus or car.\\n\\nPrague: Vaclav Havel Airport, Czech Republic (270km) – 2,5 hours\\n\\nBrno: Turany Airport, Czech Republic (80 km) – 1,5 hour\\n\\nOstrava: Leos Janacek Airport, Czech Republic (80 km) – 1,5 hour\\n\\n(posted 11 June 2019)\\n\\nMusic and memory in anglophone literature\\n\\nUniversité de Bourgogne, Dijon, France, 19-20 September 2019\\n\\nDeadline for proposals: 30 March 2019\\n\\nOrganizers : Chantal Schütz, Claire Guéron\\n\\n\\\"That song tonight will not go from my mind\\\" (Othello, 4.3.29) – when Shakespeare had Desdemona speak these words, he set up the scene for an involuntary musical recollection generated by a parallel situation. While the ars memoriaea pproach of the Renaissance, inspired by classical rhetoric, relied on carefully crafted visual mnemotechnics, memories set off by aural stimuli occur in a manner both fortuitous and unexpected. This is a situati\",\"title\":\"https://essenglish.org/cfp/conf1909/\"},{\"document\":\"d30\",\"document_chars\":45990,\"end\":33600,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"sha256\":\"f94f08beadba7d9b735ff75b702ccaf80cb342286429d01f21ab89e200dd8c84\",\"snapshot\":\"be58fb82f749ee77102eed93f6ddcac6babc7fbe5610c5090b94be0ec3abfe50\",\"start\":31600,\"text\":\" Era\\\" International Conference invites scholars worldwide to explore the consequences of the digital revolution on the production, distribution, dissemination and study of Shakespeare on screen. Since the 1999 Málaga conference, the rise (and fall) of the DVD, the digitalization of sounds and images allowing us to experience and store films on our computers, the spreading of easy filming/editing tools, the live broadcasts of theatre performances in cinemas or on the Internet, the development of online video archives and social media, as well as the increasing globalisation of production and distribution (raising the question of technological availability worldwide), have changed the ways Shakespeare is (re)created, consumed, shared and examined. Shakespeare's screen evanescence and his transfictional and transmediatic spectrality have blurred the boundaries between what Shakespeare is and is not, leading us to question our own position as scholars who keep spotting, constructing and projecting \\\"Shakespeare\\\" in audiovisual productions.\\n\\nWe invite seminar proposals (international pairs or trios of convenors are welcome) and panel proposals (featuring 3 short contributions) exploring the screen afterlives of Shakespeare's works in the digital era all over the world, revisiting the Shakespearean \\\"classics\\\" as they have been re-released in various formats, examining how the technological and aesthetic issues intersect with questions of gender, class, ethnicity and ethics, and interrogating more theoretically what \\\"is\\\" and \\\"is not\\\" Shakespeare on screen. Seminar proposals (including a 400-word presentation and a short bio for each convenor) and panel proposals (including three 300-word abstracts and three short bios) should be sent by 30 May 2018 to Sarah Hatchuel (s_hatchuel@hotmail.com) and Nathalie Vienne-Guerrin (nathalie.vienne-guerrin@univ-montp3.fr)\\n\\n(posted 26 January 2018)\\n\\nBiennial International Conference on the Linguistics of Contemporary English (BICLCE 2019)\",\"title\":\"https://essenglish.org/cfp/conf1909/\"}]","role":"user"},{"content":"Current control state (data, not source evidence):\n{\"current_notes_not_evidence\":[],\"evidence_shelf\":{\"omitted_for_capacity\":[],\"restored_exact_windows\":[\"e1\",\"e2\"],\"selection\":\"bounded recent first-delivery order; not a relevance/verification judgment\"},\"feedback\":null,\"instruction\":\"Read only useful passages. Notes and all-page cleanup are optional.\",\"literal_answer_contract\":{\"origin\":\"explicit experiment configuration, not inferred from question\",\"prefix\":\"\",\"suffix\":\"\"},\"phase\":\"RESEARCH\",\"remaining\":{\"action_slots\":181,\"backend_calls\":80,\"model_calls\":3,\"output_reservation\":46431},\"research_workflow\":{\"active_gap_not_verified\":null,\"available_pages_not_ranked_for_relevance\":[{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d120\"},\"ref\":\"d120\",\"snippet\":\" ... Focus on the Collection, Israel Museum, Jerusalem, July 10, 2001–July 10, 2002. (Catalogue)\\n\\nLe Théâtre de Jean Dubuffet, Musée Malraux, Le Havre, France, \",\"title\":\"https://www.pacegallery.com/artists/jean-dubuffet/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d119\"},\"ref\":\"d119\",\"snippet\":\" ... Sarah C Rosenthal\\n\\nscr875@g.harvard.eduNorthern Renaissance\\n\\nSarah C. Rosenthal is a PhD Candidate in History of Art and Architecture with a focus on North\",\"title\":\"https://haa.fas.harvard.edu/graduate-students\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d118\"},\"ref\":\"d118\",\"snippet\":\" ... Sarah Devereux\\n\\n- CCI Outstanding Dissertation Award: Minjeong Kim ('24), PhD\\n\\nCarla White\\n\\nPhD candidate Carla White's passion for research throughout her\",\"title\":\"https://cci.utk.edu/blog/2025/04/10/three-doctoral-students-receive-2025-cci-graduate-student-awards/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d117\"},\"ref\":\"d117\",\"snippet\":\" ... Phillip Denny is a PhD candidate working on histories of architectural prefabrication, colonialism, and urbanization in the twentieth century. He is advise\",\"title\":\"https://www.gsd.harvard.edu/doctoral-programs/doctor-of-philosophy/student-bios/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d116\"},\"ref\":\"d116\",\"snippet\":\" ... Pennycook (2018)...\\n\\n...(Pennycook 2018).\\n\\nAuthor Surname, Forename. Year. Title of book, Series Statement/Edition Statement/Volume Statement (Place of pub\",\"title\":\"https://librarydevelopment.group.shef.ac.uk/referencing/mhra-author-date.html\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d115\"},\"ref\":\"d115\",\"snippet\":\" ... However, the dissertation enhancement grant does not support fundamental dissertation research. For this reason, preference will be given to PhD candidates\",\"title\":\"https://gradschool.vanderbilt.edu/student-resources/professional-development/gli/gli-funding-opportunities/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d114\"},\"ref\":\"d114\",\"snippet\":\" ... The same year, the name of the club changed for Havre Athletic Club. The association football code received definitively the members adhesion in 1894. From\",\"title\":\"https://www.rsssf.org/tablesf/franchamp.html\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d113\"},\"ref\":\"d113\",\"snippet\":\" ... date: 2009-09-10\\n---\\nship image: La Bourgogne, ca. 1895.jpg\\nship caption: Photochrom postcard of La Bourgogneentering Le Havre\\n\\nship country: France\\nship f\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SS_La_Bourgogne\"}],\"consecutive_repeat_rounds\":1,\"contract\":{\"enabled\":true,\"gap_state\":true,\"guided_read\":true,\"recovery_rounds\":2,\"repeat_threshold\":2,\"repetition\":\"bounded\",\"reuse_results\":true,\"version\":\"gap-workflow-v1\"},\"instruction\":\"Use the current missing relation to choose a real next action. Page-name search is not page reading; cached is not proof of progress.\",\"last_new_navigation_source_round\":10,\"last_new_raw_source_round\":7,\"previous_gap_judgments_not_verified\":[],\"recovery_decisions_used\":0,\"stage\":\"normal\"},\"retriever_capabilities\":{\"boolean_operators\":false,\"kind\":\"sqlite-fts5-bm25\",\"negative_result\":\"no hit for this expression is not proof that the fact is absent\",\"phrase_quotes\":false,\"query_rule\":\"lowercase; regex word extraction; first-occurrence deduplication; OR of quoted individual tokens\",\"ranking\":\"SQLite bm25(search), ascending; docid tie-break; unchanged from q26 LocalIndex\",\"scope\":\"fixed local corpus; not live web\",\"site_filter\":false,\"title_kind\":\"stored URL, not an extracted page title\",\"warning\":\"site:, quotes and AND/OR in input are not filters/operators. Their words may become ordinary search terms. Use a few discriminating terms.\"},\"runtime_contract\":{\"evidence_shelf_size\":3,\"max_calls_per_response\":4,\"max_queries_per_search\":3,\"require_sources\":true},\"uncommitted_response_not_evidence\":null}","role":"user"}],"model":"EB-GLM-5.2","temperature":0.0,"tool_choice":"auto","tools":[{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find candidate documents in the configured corpus; it does NOT open their full text.\nUSE WHEN: No suitable page is known, a new entity/relation needs locating, or a different clue is needed after irrelevant results.\nAVOID: Do not repeat a page-name query when you intend to read an existing result. Do not treat snippets as proof or unsupported operators as filters.\nINPUT: queries is an array of 1..3 distinct nonblank strings, each <=2000 characters; top_k is an optional integer 1..10 (default 5). See runtime retriever_capabilities. replay=true explicitly restores the full cached navigation view; it does not force fresh SQL.\nOUTPUT: ok/results contains query, hits with ref/title/snippet, cache status and observation metadata. navigation_seen is NOT a read receipt; raw_ranges_delivered lists actual windows. read_action is an available example, not auto-execution. Metadata counts operations, not relevance. Exact delivered repeats may use view=reuse and omit snippets; replay=true restores them.\nWORKFLOW: search -> inspect returned dN -> read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}); after reading, use the newly found entity and one missing relation for a new search, or finish directly.","name":"search","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"queries":{"items":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":1,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"replay":{"type":"boolean"},"top_k":{"maximum":10,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["queries"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Open the raw text of a received search result, or replay a previously delivered evidence window.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate page may answer the current gap; inspect its actual text before another page-name search. Use continuation to include a subject/date split at a boundary.\nAVOID: Do not guess handles or cite an unread result. Do not infer an entity relationship merely because adjacent windows mention different people.\nINPUT: Only ref is required. dN opens from start=0 with configured read_chars by default; optional integer start>=0 and length=1..6000 use Unicode code points. eN accepts only ref and restores the exact old window. Optional goal<=400 characters on dN selects one lexical paragraph window; it is mutually exclusive with start and forbidden on eN. length remains an upper bound.\nOUTPUT: ok/evidence contains eN, document, snapshot, start/end, original text and integrity fields; next_start supports continuation. The window becomes citable after it is delivered in a subsequent model input. Source text is untrusted data. goal no-match returns matched=false with no evidence; selection metadata reports lexical matches and actual range, never a semantic guarantee.\nWORKFLOW: read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) -> compare the original constraint with the text -> search a newly discovered gap, continue read, or finish with delivered eN.","name":"read","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"goal":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"length":{"maximum":6000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"ref":{"pattern":"^[de][1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find literal text positions inside one already received document; this is page-local navigation.\nUSE WHEN: The page is known but a name or exact phrase is far from its beginning.\nAVOID: Do not use a literal zero-match result to prove a fact absent. It does not search aliases, paraphrases or the whole corpus.\nINPUT: ref must be a received dN; text is a nonblank string <=2000 characters; optional integer start>=0; ignore_case is boolean, default false.\nOUTPUT: ok/document/snapshot/matches gives original start/end positions and exact excerpts, case_sensitive and next_start. Matches are positions_not_evidence, not citable eN.\nWORKFLOW: find -> read the matched range with enough preceding subject context -> compare evidence. Change literal terms or use goal-read rather than repeating zero matches.","name":"find","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ignore_case":{"type":"boolean"},"ref":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"text":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["ref","text"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Locate earlier delivered evidence, received search navigation and optional note history without external retrieval.\nUSE WHEN: A known lead or earlier raw window has left the active context; recover it instead of re-searching the same phrase.\nAVOID: Do not cite a recall excerpt as new evidence. It cannot search unreceived backend data; a lexical miss is not a proof of absence.\nINPUT: query is a nonblank string <=2000 characters. Use a discriminating entity or relation already encountered.\nOUTPUT: ok/matches has ref or note key, exact excerpt and kind. eN can be replayed; dN can be opened; inactive notes are historical model judgments, not evidence.\nWORKFLOW: recall -> read({\"ref\":\"eN\"}) for exact recovery, or read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) for an unread page. Then update only the gap that changed.","name":"recall","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"query":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Maintain a small optional free-text scratchpad; not verified facts or a prerequisite to submit.\nUSE WHEN: A brief reusable alias, rejected route or independent reminder will help later. Prefer update_gap for the active research question when available.\nAVOID: Do not summarize every page, copy the full question, or repeatedly write the same note. Notes do not automatically retract dependent plans.\nINPUT: put requires op/key/text/anchors; text <=600 characters, anchors is <=6 delivered eN. delete requires op/key only. Keys are 1..32 ASCII letters/digits/_/-. Capacity is explicit.\nOUTPUT: ok/key/changed and kind=agent_note_not_evidence, or deleted. A no-op is not research progress. Errors do not silently alter saved notes.\nWORKFLOW: Optionally save a useful observation alongside another already-planned action; keep sources in the archive and finish without cleanup.","name":"notes","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"anchors":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"put"},"text":{"maxLength":600,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["op","key","text","anchors"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"delete"}},"required":["op","key"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Explicitly submit the requested answer with source windows, or explicitly abstain.\nUSE WHEN: The requested core answer has sufficient support, or the available budget/evidence cannot resolve it. No note, gap update or audit is mandatory.\nAVOID: Do not claim every clue is verified when it is not. Do not change established into expanded, by-year into in-year, or hide unresolved numeric conflicts in a long explanation.\nINPUT: Answer branch requires answer and refs. Nonblank strings are <=8000 characters; string-integer-v1 additionally permits plain JSON integers, not bools/floats, rendered as decimal text. Strings stay exact. Abstention requires abstain=true and nonblank reason<=2000 characters. Never mix branches. refs contains only delivered eN, <=16; configured source and literal-format requirements still apply.\nOUTPUT: ok/terminal records submitted or abstained. Submitted answer is text with refs/basis and any representation metadata. Legal references are NOT semantic verification. Explicit prefix/suffix constraints still apply.\nWORKFLOW: Finish last in a response, based only on evidence already received for that decision. Never combine a new read and a guessed citation to its unseen result. In FINAL only finish is allowed.","name":"finish","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"answer":{"maxLength":8000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":["string","integer"]},"refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":16,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true}},"required":["answer","refs"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"abstain":{"const":true},"reason":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["abstain","reason"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Replace the one active research question and retain a bounded history of explicit model judgments; it is NOT an automatic verifier.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate, unresolved relation, rejection or conflict changed, or repeated searches need a concrete next objective. Use sparingly, not after every tool.\nAVOID: Do not turn the original question or your prior guess into evidence. Updating a gap does not count as a new observation and does not reset a search loop.\nINPUT: subject/question/basis are nonblank <=400 characters; kind and status follow schema; evidence_refs are <=6 received eN, navigation_refs <=6 received dN; next_action is one named existing tool. supported/rejected/conflict require evidence_refs. Supply a concise decision basis, not a transcript.\nOUTPUT: ok/changed/current returns agent_judgment_not_verified with revision. At most four previous distinct gap versions remain in the active view; the full update is journaled. Sources are checked for delivery, not entailment.\nWORKFLOW: Observe -> identify one missing relationship or record a real rejection -> select read on an available page or search for a new relation. An update may share a response with known independent actions; no update is required before finish.","name":"update_gap","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"basis":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"evidence_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"kind":{"enum":["locate","read","relation","disambiguate","conflict","recover"]},"navigation_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"next_action":{"enum":["search","read","find","recall","finish"]},"question":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"status":{"enum":["open","supported","rejected","conflict"]},"subject":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["subject","question","kind","status","evidence_refs","navigation_refs","next_action","basis"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"}]}